Assembler Version 03
====================
Assembled by: Version 02

Features Supported by This Assembler
-------------------------------------
This version adds label constant assignments, origin setting, and byte
selectors for extracting the low or high byte of a label's value. These
features lay the groundwork for the next version to use named zero-page
variables and set the program origin.

Instruction mnemonics (expanded from version 02):
  ADC# ADCZ ASLA BCC BCS BEQ BNE BRK CLC CMPZ,X CMP# CMP,Y DEY INCZ INX
  INY JMP JSR LDAZ LDA# LDA(),Y LDA,Y LDX# LDY# ORAZ RTS SBC# SBCZ SEC
  STA STA(),Y STAZ STAZ,X TYA

  New instructions: BITZ (BIT zero-page), BMI, BPL, SBCZ (SBC zero-page)

DATA directive:
  DATA $XX ...        - emit hex bytes
  DATA "string"       - emit ASCII string with \n and \\ escapes
  DATA $XXXX          - emit 16-bit value (little-endian)
  Mixed: DATA $XX "string" $XXXX on same line

Operand types in instruction arguments:
  $XX                 - 8-bit hex value
  $XXXX               - 16-bit hex value (little-endian)
  "string"            - ASCII string with \n, \\, and \" escapes
  label               - 16-bit label reference (little-endian)
  <label              - low byte of label value (1 byte emitted)
  >label              - high byte of label value (1 byte emitted)

Label features:
  - Labels at column 0 bound to program counter
  - label = $XXXX     - constant assignment (hex value only)
  - * = $XXXX         - set program counter (origin directive)
  - Linear search through label table at $3000
  - Forward references NOT supported (single-pass)
  - Duplicate label detection

Error handling:
  - Error 01: Label not found
  - Error 02: Duplicate label
  - Error 03: Opcode not found
  - Error 04: Expected hex value

Semicolon comments (to end of line).
Output starts at $2000 (hardcoded in source).

New in this version (relative to version 02):
- < (low byte) selector for label operands
- > (high byte) selector for label operands
- label = $XXXX constant assignments
- * = $XXXX origin/program counter setting
- New instructions: BITZ, BMI, BPL, SBCZ
- Separate findlabel and readandfindexistinglabel helper functions
- Improved checkforend with common path for ; and newline
- New error code for missing hex values

Features Used in This Assembler's Source Code
----------------------------------------------
The source uses the same feature set as version 02 provides. Despite adding
< and > byte selectors and label = $XXXX assignments, the source itself does
not use these new features. Zero-page variables are still referenced by raw
hex addresses (e.g., $02 instead of <TABL), and constants are listed as
comments rather than actual assignments.

Source features used:
  - Non-standard instruction mnemonics (from version 02's table)
  - Labels at column 0 for code locations
  - Label references as 16-bit operands
  - DATA directive with hex bytes and string literals
  - Hex operands ($XX and $XXXX)
  - String character literals in operands (e.g., CMP# "\n", CMP# "\\")
  - Semicolon comments
  - Branch targets as hardcoded hex offsets

New syntax used in source (relative to version 02):
- Character escape literals used directly in instruction operands
  (e.g., CMP# "\n" instead of CMP# $0A, CMP# "\\" instead of CMP# $5C,
  CMP# "\"" instead of CMP# $22). While technically supported by version 01
  as string operands, this is the first version to use them extensively in
  instruction operands for readability.
